From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: don't hold for a dry cache with the film demuxed
 far ahead

Right after a start the source cache reads empty: the demuxer has just
taken everything it held, and is already tens of seconds past the clock.
The source-underrun hold took that for a dry source and paused playback
for 180 ms, 1.7 s into the film; the audio queued in the sink ran past
the stopped clock and the engine's correction after it dropped a frame.

Skip the hold while the last demuxed video packet is more than 10 s past
the clock. A source that really has gone away still gets its hold, once
the demuxed runway has come down to that.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -2289,6 +2289,8 @@ constexpr double SRC_UNDERRUN_WATCH = 2.
 constexpr auto SRC_PROBE_INTERVAL = 50ms;
 // The player's own buffering leaves the cache dry too, so wait this long after it.
 constexpr auto SRC_UNDERRUN_COOLDOWN = 5000ms;
+// Demuxed this far past the clock, playback has its own runway whatever the cache says.
+constexpr double SRC_DEMUXED_AHEAD = 10.0;
 } // unnamed namespace
 
 CacheInfo CVideoPlayer::GetCachingTimes()
@@ -2374,6 +2376,11 @@ bool CVideoPlayer::TryEnterSourceUnderru
   if (!m_processInfo->GetVideoCodecBuffersData())
     return false;
 
+  // A start reads the cache as empty because the demuxer has just taken all of it.
+  if (m_CurrentVideo.dts != DVD_NOPTS_VALUE &&
+      m_CurrentVideo.dts - m_clock.GetClock() > DVD_SEC_TO_TIME(SRC_DEMUXED_AHEAD))
+    return false;
+
   // Reading the status takes the cache's locks and clears its slow-source flag.
   if (!m_srcUnderrunProbe.IsTimePast())
     return false;
